delta_from_prior:
LFQ (00036) still chose forms and fresh variables by matroid greedy, relied on the 2^n enumeration certificate, and had no answer to stabilizer-free extra clauses. New here:
- the basis is removed altogether (pivot-zero section), so greedy incompatibility cannot occur;
- an exact residual invariant w with a tight threshold and a constructive lift;
- a syntactic polynomial certificate replacing complete enumeration;
- a hardness conjecture for discovery in place of a completeness hope;
- a fixture combining an overlapping-form block with stabilizer-free residual clauses, and the majority-lift adversary against RTS itself.
Not new: root-only scope and the hidden linear lift family.
